WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.987
An S M executes the threads in a block in
groups called warps.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:09.950
In the eight rows by thirty-two columns
case, the block has one warp.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.789
Each lane identifies one thread in that
warp.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.303
A word offset counts four byte values from
the start of the array.

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:20.629
The first eight lanes read consecutive
columns.

00:00:20.809 --> 00:00:23.921
Their eight values fit in one thirty-two
byte sector.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.244
The transpose swaps row and column.

00:00:27.424 --> 00:00:31.035
In the output, these lanes write eight
words apart.

00:00:31.215 --> 00:00:34.709
The same eight lanes now touch eight
distinct sectors.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:41.057
Across all lanes, the addresses cover four
read sectors and thirty-two write sectors.

00:00:41.237 --> 00:00:43.606
The calculation groups addresses.

00:00:43.786 --> 00:00:49.939
Measured GPU traffic also depends on caches
and the instructions the hardware runs.
